  "title": "Retire remaining Ollama provider, semantic-model, fault-vocabulary and directory residue after B154 retirement and sibling-provision convergence",
  "summary": "Amendments b154-ollama-retirement-20261002 (rev 235) and ollama-sibling-residue-20261002-r2 (rev 238) are executed: B154 is retired, sibling provisions no longer grant Ollama authority, and the ollama module/formal-rule/metadata rows read retired. Residue remains outside the scope of both: local_model_provider_registry still registers provider OLLAMA_LOCAL as status=active although B154 states the retired service holds no active authority; semantic_model_registry keeps three OLLAMA_LOCAL embedding/reranker bindings at status=observed; current_normative_surface still lists formal-rule:FR-OLLAMA-ON-DEMAND as lifecycle_state=active while the rule itself is retired; final_implementation_inventory row INV_LOCAL_MODEL remains status=current; ten OLLAMA_* fault codes in fault_code_directory are still un-retired active vocabulary for a runtime that no longer exists, and the active-authoritative-inventory enumerations in test_flow_directory.TF_GLOBAL_FAULT_DIRECTORY_COVERAGE.fixtures and maintenance_manual_directory.GLOBAL_FAULT_CONTAINMENT_AND_ROUTING.applicable_fault_codes still list them; fault code MODEL_RUNTIME_NOT_READY still names Ollama in its trigger; project_architecture_directory.PROJECT_GPTBRIDGE.dependencies still lists registered-Ollama-C-drive-paths; article C27 still enumerates Ollama as a connection type. The executed r2 amendment explicitly deferred the inventory-state convergence and the fault-code traceability decision; this request performs the provider/vocabulary/traceability side of that convergence while the governor-held observation reconciliation governs the local_model_registry/model_residency_registry observation rows. Codex-law and registry convergence only; no implementation change.",
  "requested_by": "decision-sovereign",
  "origin": "convergence pass after executed b154-ollama-retirement-20261002 and ollama-sibling-residue-20261002-r2; r2 acceptance out_of_scope recorded OLLAMA_* fault vocabulary retirement as a separate traceability decision and model-registry restamp as a separate inventory-state convergence; r1/r2 closed stale because concurrent amendments advanced the authority past the r1 predecessor (rev 241) - r3 re-anchors to rev 242",
  "problem": {
    "summary": "Post-retirement residue: provider OLLAMA_LOCAL still active; 3 semantic model bindings still observed for the retired provider; formal-rule surface entry still active after rule retirement; inventory row INV_LOCAL_MODEL still current; 10 OLLAMA_* fault codes un-retired and still enumerated in the global fault-coverage flow and maintenance manual; MODEL_RUNTIME_NOT_READY trigger still names Ollama; PROJECT_GPTBRIDGE dependencies still list Ollama C-drive paths; C27 still enumerates Ollama as a connection type.",
